% ============================================================================
% food-group-alternative-form.query.adj — a worked recall over the
% nutrition food-group-alternative-form library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "does juice count as a
% fruit?": it states no nutrition fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `food_group_alternative_form` rows and returns the
% alternative form + the table's source/locator/trust. Grains, whose own
% cited definitional sentence names no comparable alternative form,
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli food-group-alternative-form.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "food-group-alternative-form.adj"

? food_group_alternative_form(fruits, $Form)                              % expect hundred_percent_fruit_juice
? food_group_alternative_form($Group, hundred_percent_vegetable_juice)     % expect vegetables
? food_group_alternative_form(grains, $Form)                              % expect abstain — grains' own cited span names no alternative form
